[[2047,31,0,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The headlamp alignment device in \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is supplied at pin\n3 by a line coming from the circuit for the dipped beam headlamps,\nprotected by fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F5</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the junction unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B1</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ;  this\nline only supplies voltage to the regulator when the dipped beam\nheadlamps are switched on. (\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3233782\">E2011</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              )\nthis line provides voltage to the regulator only when the dipped\nbeams are on.</p><p>Pin 4 of device \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is earthed, whilst\npin 2 sends the signal to adjust the motors \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N30</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               (left) and \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N31</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               (right),\nthrough a resistive divider which alters the output voltage depending\non which of the four positions has been selected.</p><p>Motors \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N30</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N31</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               contain\na transducer that establishes actual motor travel on the basis of\nthe voltage of an adjustment signal received by pin 2 from device \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .\nThe motors are supplied through pins 3 from the line (part of the dipped\nbeam circuit) that supplies device \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , while pins 1 are\nearthed.</p><p>The headlamp alignment device \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is\nlit up (at pin 1) when the side lights are switched on by means\nof the line coming from the switch for the steering column switch\nunit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H5</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and protected by the controls illumination fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B11</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               up to\n2/99 or fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F4</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the additional fuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98B</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               from\n2/99.</p>"]]